// php.ungram — Mahout syntax-tree schema for PHP 8.5
// =====================================================================
// This file is the single source of truth for the shape of the
// syntax tree. `build.rs` generates from it: the SyntaxKind enum, one
// struct per node with named child fields, the alternation enums, and
// the mixin traits (ADR-0003; design §4.9).
// It is the change-controlled artifact named in the M0 plan (§8): freely
// churned until gate G8, ADR-per-change after. The normative grammar of
// PHP remains php-src's zend_language_parser.y + the differential gates;
// this file records the *tree we build*, which may be more permissive
// than PHP (see the VALIDATE marker convention below).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DSL SYNTAX
//   Node = Rule                  struct node: SyntaxKind + a struct of fields
//   Node = A | B | C             alternation-only: generates a typed enum
//   trait Name = Rule            mixin (see A5)
//   Node : TraitA TraitB = Rule  node opts into mixins
//   juxtaposition = sequence;  (…) grouping;  ?  optional;  *  zero-or-more
//   R,*  /  R,+   comma-separated list, zero-/one-or-more, trailing comma ok
//   'kw'          literal token (keywords written lowercase; the lexer is
//                 case-insensitive, so 'function' matches FUNCTION etc.)
//   <class>       token class (see TOKEN CLASSES)
//   label:Rule    names the generated field
//   l:R (sep l:R)*  one label at a list's head and in its tail is one
//                 list field (a head-and-tail list is not two fields)
//   Rule!         REQUIRED child (see A2)
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// CONVENTIONS
//
// A1 — Nodes and enums. Every struct node maps 1:1 to a SyntaxKind.
//   Alternation-only definitions generate enums (e.g. `Expr`, `Stmt`)
//   whose variants are the listed nodes; token-only alternations
//   (e.g. `BinaryOp`) generate a token accessor + kind predicate.
//
// A2 — Arity honesty (the recovery contract). DEFAULT IS OPTIONAL:
//   every child field is Option<T> unless marked `!`, because under
//   error recovery any child can be absent. `Rule!` is a promise
//   ENFORCED ON THE PARSER, and the field is the bare type, so the tree
//   builder cannot construct the node without that child. Use `!` only
//   where construction is anchored on the child itself (a BinaryExpr is
//   built *around* an existing lhs; a PostfixIncDec around its operand)
//   or on a token that cannot appear without it. Repetition (`*`, `,*`,
//   `,+`) generates a boxed slice — possibly empty even for `,+`; the
//   `+` records grammar intent and seeds a validation diagnostic.
//   (M0.3 refinement: `!` markers were audited against the real parser's
//   recovery paths and removed wherever construction is NOT anchored on
//   the child — e.g. a do-while is built from `do`, so its body can be
//   absent under recovery. The survivors are hard guarantees.)
//
// A3 — Tokens. Literal tokens stay in the token stream (lossless) and
//   become fields only when labeled or when the node is token-only.
//   Multiple alternative tokens in one position (e.g. op:('+'|'-'))
//   generate a single token field whose kind the caller inspects.
//
// A4 — Same-typed siblings. When a node has several children of one
//   type, the builder resolves the labeled fields POSITIONALLY RELATIVE
//   TO ANCHOR TOKENS in the rule (e.g. TernaryExpr's `then` is the Expr between
//   '?' and ':'; `else_branch` follows ':'). Where optionality would
//   make anchored positions ambiguous, a wrapper node is introduced
//   instead (ForInit/ForCond/ForStep, ForeachKey, ArrayKey, YieldKey).
//   Wrappers are deliberate API, not noise: they give lowering a stable
//   place to hang spans.
//
// A5 — Mixins. `trait` definitions inject their children as fields of
//   every opted-in node and generate a Rust trait that reads them, so
//   the compiler generalizes over HasAttributes/HasModifiers/etc.
//   instead of matching node-by-node. HasDocComment is the one
//   trivia-backed trait: it declares no children; the field it injects
//   is the token index of the doc comment the node took, at the position
//   of the grammar where php's backup_doc_comment stands (the parser
//   emits the take there; the builder's docs say what php's rule is).
//
// A6 — Trivia. Whitespace and comments are trivia tokens: present in
//   the token stream (losslessness), invisible to this schema and to
//   the typed nodes. Inline HTML is NOT trivia — it has echo semantics —
//   and is modeled as InlineHtmlStmt below. Open/close tags ('<?php',
//   '?>') are structural tokens owned by the nodes they delimit; the
//   `?>`-as-semicolon rule is a parser token-glue rule, not a schema
//   concern. (NOTE: design doc §5.1 loosely called HTML segments trivia;
//   this file is the precise statement and the doc will be amended.)
//
// A7 — Markers used in comments below:
//   DESUGAR:  this node is an HIR lowering input with a known desugar
//   VALIDATE: the tree is more permissive than PHP here; the named
//             rejection lives in the validation pass (M0 plan §4.4.4)
//   LEVEL:    construct gated on LanguageLevel (min PHP version)
//   NOTE:     rationale / conformance trap worth knowing at the schema
//
// A8 — Naming. Nodes CamelCase with suffix conventions: *Expr, *Stmt,
//   *Decl, *Type, *Clause, *List. SyntaxKind names are the SCREAMING
//   form, generated.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// TOKEN CLASSES (full token set is generated; see conformance/token_map.md)
//   <ident>          identifier (not a variable)
//   <member_ident>   <ident> ∪ semi-reserved keywords — legal in member-
//                    name position (methods, class consts, enum cases,
//                    property names after ->, named-arg labels).
//                    NOTE: 'class' is excluded as a const name; the
//                    contextual-keyword module is the runtime authority.
//   <variable>       '$' + name token ($x)
//   <name_qualified> <name_fully_qualified> <name_relative>
//                    A\B   \A\B   namespace\A   (php 8.0 single tokens)
//   <int> <float>    numeric literals (underscores, 0x/0b/0o/legacy octal)
//   <single_quoted>  complete single-quoted string (incl. b'…')
//   <string_text>    literal run inside "…", heredoc, nowdoc, `…`
//   <heredoc_start> <heredoc_end>   <<<LABEL / closing label (both
//                    heredoc and nowdoc variants; flexible-indent strip
//                    records are trivia attached here)
//   <encaps_int>     integer in the restricted in-string dim grammar
//   <magic_const>    __LINE__ __FILE__ __DIR__ __FUNCTION__ __CLASS__
//                    __TRAIT__ __METHOD__ __NAMESPACE__ __PROPERTY__?
//                    (set is generated; case-insensitive)
//   <cast>           '(int)' … '(object)' incl. interior whitespace
//   <cast_removed>   '(real)' / '(unset)'  → targeted MHT diagnostic
//   <inline_html>    verbatim HTML segment
//   <halt_data>      everything after __halt_compiler();
//   <open_tag_echo>  '<?='
//
// =====================================================================

// ----- mixins ---------------------------------------------------------

trait HasAttributes = attrs:AttributeGroup*
trait HasModifiers  = modifiers:Modifier*
trait HasDocComment =            // trivia-backed; see A5

// ----- source structure ----------------------------------------------

SourceFile = Stmt*
// NOTE: a file may begin/end mid-HTML; leading <inline_html> before the
// first '<?php' is an InlineHtmlStmt like any other.

InlineHtmlStmt = body:<inline_html>     // DESUGAR: echo of a constant

HaltCompilerStmt = '__halt_compiler' '(' ')' ';' data:<halt_data>?
// NOTE: Composer/phar stubs; data participates in G2 losslessness.

StmtList = Stmt*    // body of alternative-syntax constructs

// ----- names and references ------------------------------------------

NameRef = <ident> | <name_qualified> | <name_fully_qualified> | <name_relative>
// NOTE: resolution is M1; 'true','false','null','self','parent','static',
// 'never','mixed', class names — all arrive here undifferentiated.

MemberName = name:<member_ident>

// ----- types ----------------------------------------------------------

TypeExpr = NamedType | NullableType | UnionType | IntersectionType | ParenType

NamedType        = name:NameRef!
NullableType     = '?' ty:TypeExpr
UnionType        = types:TypeExpr ('|' types:TypeExpr)*
IntersectionType = types:TypeExpr ('&' types:TypeExpr)*   // LEVEL: 8.1
ParenType        = '(' ty:TypeExpr ')'             // LEVEL: 8.2 (DNF)
// VALIDATE: DNF shape rules (no nested unions in parens, no duplicate
// members); nullable cannot wrap union/intersection.
// NOTE: '(A&B)|C' vs parenthesized expression in parameter position is
// a parser disambiguation; the 8.1 ampersand token split (M0 §4.2)
// resolves 'A&B $x' vs 'A &$x' before the parser sees it.

// ----- attributes ------------------------------------------------------

AttributeGroup = '#[' Attribute,+ ']'
Attribute      = name:NameRef! args:ArgList?
// NOTE: argument expressions stored as-is; item tree keeps spans only.

// ----- modifiers --------------------------------------------------------

Modifier = 'public' | 'protected' | 'private'
         | SetVisibility
         | 'static' | 'abstract' | 'final' | 'readonly' | 'var'
// VALIDATE: duplicate/conflicting modifiers; 'var' legacy property-only.

SetVisibility = vis:('public' | 'protected' | 'private') '(' 'set' ')'
// LEVEL: 8.4. NOTE: four tokens glued in modifier position only;
// 'private(set)' elsewhere is a call — contextual-keyword module owns this.

// ----- statements -------------------------------------------------------

Stmt = Block | ExprStmt | EmptyStmt | InlineHtmlStmt | HaltCompilerStmt
     | IfStmt | WhileStmt | DoWhileStmt | ForStmt | ForeachStmt | SwitchStmt
     | BreakStmt | ContinueStmt | ReturnStmt | GotoStmt | LabelStmt
     | TryStmt | EchoStmt | GlobalStmt | StaticVarStmt | UnsetStmt
     | ConstStmt | UseStmt | NamespaceDef | DeclareStmt
     | FunctionDecl | ClassDecl | InterfaceDecl | TraitDecl | EnumDecl
// NOTE: declarations are statements in PHP (conditional declaration is
// the language model — design doc §6.1); the item tree extracts the
// declaration subset and marks conditionality by nesting.

Block     = '{' Stmt* '}'
ExprStmt  = expr:Expr! ';'        // ';' may be supplied by '?>' glue
EmptyStmt = ';'

IfStmt = 'if' '(' cond:Expr ')'
         ( then:Stmt ElseifClause* ElseClause?
         | ':' StmtList AltElseifClause* AltElseClause? 'endif' ';' )
ElseifClause    = 'elseif' '(' cond:Expr ')' body:Stmt
ElseClause      = 'else' body:Stmt
AltElseifClause = 'elseif' '(' cond:Expr ')' ':' StmtList
AltElseClause   = 'else' ':' StmtList
// NOTE: 'else if' (two words) parses as ElseClause{ IfStmt } — by design,
// matching php-src. VALIDATE: 'else if' illegal in alternative syntax.

WhileStmt   = 'while' '(' cond:Expr ')' ( body:Stmt | ':' StmtList 'endwhile' ';' )
DoWhileStmt = 'do' body:Stmt 'while' '(' cond:Expr ')' ';'

ForStmt = 'for' '(' init:ForInit ';' cond:ForCond ';' step:ForStep ')'
          ( body:Stmt | ':' StmtList 'endfor' ';' )
ForInit = Expr,*        // wrappers per A4; each may be empty
ForCond = Expr,*        // NOTE: comma lists — last cond decides (DESUGAR)
ForStep = Expr,*

ForeachStmt = 'foreach' '(' iterable:Expr 'as' key:ForeachKey? target:ForeachTarget? ')'
              ( body:Stmt | ':' StmtList 'endforeach' ';' )
ForeachKey    = key:Expr! '=>'
ForeachTarget = byref:'&'? target:Expr
// DESUGAR: iterator protocol (design doc §7.1). VALIDATE: target must be
// writable / destructurable; by-ref target excludes key-less list forms.

SwitchStmt = 'switch' '(' subject:Expr ')'
             ( '{' SwitchArm* '}' | ':' SwitchArm* 'endswitch' ';' )
SwitchArm  = ('case' value:Expr | 'default') (':' | ';') StmtList
// NOTE: ';' after case/default is legal, archaic, and in the corpus.

BreakStmt    = 'break' level:Expr? ';'
ContinueStmt = 'continue' level:Expr? ';'
// VALIDATE: level must be a positive integer literal (since PHP 5.4).

ReturnStmt = 'return' value:Expr? ';'
GotoStmt   = 'goto' label:<ident> ';'
LabelStmt  = name:<ident>! ':'

TryStmt       = 'try' body:Block! CatchClause* FinallyClause?
CatchClause   = 'catch' '(' types:CatchTypeList var:<variable>? ')' body:Block
CatchTypeList = types:NameRef ('|' types:NameRef)*
FinallyClause = 'finally' body:Block
// VALIDATE: try requires ≥1 catch or finally. NOTE: capture-less catch is 8.0.

EchoStmt = ('echo' | <open_tag_echo>) exprs:Expr,+ ';'
// NOTE: '<?= $x ?>' — the ';' is supplied by '?>' glue; echo of several
// comma-separated values is one statement. DESUGAR: output op per value.

// NOTE: vars are the simple-variable family only ($x, $$x, ${expr} —
// Zend's simple_variable); the parser enforces it (burn-down 2026-06-11).
GlobalStmt    = 'global' vars:Expr,+ ';'
StaticVarStmt = 'static' StaticVarDeclarator,+ ';'
StaticVarDeclarator = var:<variable>! ('=' init:Expr)?
// NOTE: 'static' here vs 'static::' vs static closures/fns vs the
// modifier — four contextual readings; the decision procedure is
// centralized (M0 §4.4.3) and this node is only built for the declarator
// form. DESUGAR: per-function static slot.

UnsetStmt = 'unset' '(' targets:Expr,+ ')' ';'

ConstStmt       = 'const' ConstDeclarator,+ ';'
// NOTE: top-level const — untyped; typed constants are class-level (8.3).

UseStmt      = 'use' kind:('function' | 'const')? ( UseGroup | UseClause,+ ) ';'
UseClause    = name:NameRef! alias:UseAlias?
UseAlias     = 'as' name:<ident>!
UseGroup     = prefix:NameRef! '\\' '{' UseGroupItem,+ '}'
UseGroupItem = kind:('function' | 'const')? name:NameRef! alias:UseAlias?
// VALIDATE: kind-on-statement and kind-on-item are mutually exclusive.

NamespaceDef = 'namespace' name:NameRef? ( body:Block | ';' )
// VALIDATE: braced and unbraced forms cannot mix in one file; unnamed
// namespace requires braced form.

DeclareStmt      = 'declare' '(' DeclareDirective,+ ')' ( body:Stmt | ':' StmtList 'enddeclare' ';' | ';' )
DeclareDirective = name:<ident>! '=' value:Expr
// VALIDATE: strict_types value/placement (first statement, no block form).

// ----- declarations -----------------------------------------------------

FunctionDecl : HasAttributes HasDocComment =
    'function' byref:'&'? name:<ident>! params:ParamList! ret:RetType? body:Block

RetType   = ':' ty:TypeExpr
ParamList = '(' Param,* ')'

Param : HasAttributes HasModifiers =
    ty:TypeExpr? byref:'&'? variadic:'...'? var:<variable>!
    ('=' default:Expr)? hooks:PropertyHookList?
// NOTE: modifiers present ⇒ constructor promotion (8.0); hooks on a
// param are legal only when promoted (8.4) — VALIDATE both, plus:
// variadic excludes default, by-ref-variadic ordering, required-after-
// optional deprecation, readonly promoted needs visibility.

ClassDecl : HasAttributes HasModifiers HasDocComment =
    'class' name:<ident>? extends:ExtendsClause? implements:ImplementsClause?
    body:ClassBody!
// VALIDATE: legal modifier set {abstract, final, readonly}; abstract+final
// conflict; readonly class member rules (8.2/8.3).

InterfaceDecl : HasAttributes HasDocComment =
    'interface' name:<ident>? extends:ExtendsClause? body:ClassBody!
TraitDecl : HasAttributes HasDocComment =
    'trait' name:<ident>? body:ClassBody!
EnumDecl : HasAttributes HasDocComment =
    'enum' name:<ident>? backing:EnumBacking? implements:ImplementsClause?
    body:ClassBody!                                  // LEVEL: 8.1
EnumBacking = ':' ty:TypeExpr
// NOTE: 'enum' is NOT reserved — this node exists only when the
// contextual lookahead fires (M0 §4.4.3). VALIDATE: backing type must be
// int|string; enums take no extends.

ExtendsClause    = 'extends' types:NameRef,+
// NOTE: shared by classes (exactly one — VALIDATE) and interfaces (many).
ImplementsClause = 'implements' types:NameRef,+

ClassBody   = '{' ClassMember* '}'
ClassMember = ClassConstDecl | PropertyDecl | MethodDecl | TraitUseDecl
            | EnumCaseDecl

ClassConstDecl : HasAttributes HasModifiers =
    'const' ty:TypeExpr? ConstDeclarator,+ ';'       // typed: LEVEL 8.3
ConstDeclarator : HasDocComment = name:MemberName! '=' value:Expr
// NOTE: semi-reserved names legal ('const FOR = 1'); 'class' excluded.
// The doc comment is the declarator's, not the statement's: php's
// class_const_decl and const_decl each end in backup_doc_comment, so in
// `/** K */ const C = 1, D = 2;` only C carries K (probed 8.5.9 with
// ReflectionClassConstant::getDocComment()).
// Initializers stay unevaluated expressions through M0 (item tree keeps
// spans; const-expr evaluation is M1).

PropertyDecl : HasAttributes HasModifiers =
    ty:TypeExpr? PropertyDeclarator,+ ( ';' | hooks:PropertyHookList )
PropertyDeclarator : HasDocComment = var:<variable>! ('=' init:Expr)?
// NOTE: the doc comment is the declarator's, as php's property rule takes
// it: `/** P */ public $x, $y;` gives P to $x alone (probed 8.5.9 with
// ReflectionProperty::getDocComment()).
// VALIDATE: hooks ⇒ exactly one declarator and no 'readonly'; typed
// property rules; 'var' excludes other visibility.

MethodDecl : HasAttributes HasModifiers HasDocComment =
    'function' byref:'&'? name:MemberName? params:ParamList! ret:RetType?
    ( body:Block | ';' )
// VALIDATE: abstract/interface methods take ';', others a body;
// __construct return type; magic-method signatures.

TraitUseDecl        = 'use' traits:NameRef,+ ( ';' | adaptations:TraitAdaptationList )
TraitAdaptationList = '{' TraitAdaptation* '}'
TraitAdaptation     = InsteadofAdaptation | AsAdaptation
InsteadofAdaptation = ref:TraitMethodRef! 'insteadof' excluded:NameRef,+ ';'
AsAdaptation        = ref:TraitMethodRef! 'as'
                      vis:('public' | 'protected' | 'private' | 'static'
                           | 'abstract' | 'final' | 'readonly')?
                      alias:MemberName? ';'
// NOTE: php-src member_modifier — `m as final;` changes the modifier, no
// alias (adjudicated via Reflection, M0.4 fixture round).
TraitMethodRef      = (trait:NameRef '::')? method:MemberName
// VALIDATE: AsAdaptation needs vis or alias (or both); insteadof needs
// the qualified ref form.

EnumCaseDecl : HasAttributes HasDocComment =
    'case' name:MemberName ('=' value:Expr)? ';'    // LEVEL: 8.1

PropertyHookList = '{' PropertyHook* '}'              // LEVEL: 8.4
PropertyHook : HasAttributes HasModifiers =
    byref:'&'? name:<ident>! params:ParamList?
    ( body:Block | arrow:HookArrowBody | ';' )
HookArrowBody = '=>' value:Expr ';'
// VALIDATE: name ∈ {get,set} (contextual idents); 'final' is the only
// legal modifier; '&' on get only; set's optional ParamList is exactly
// one param, no default (typing must MATCH the property: an untyped
// property requires an untyped set param — upstream manual, adjudicated
// M0.4; the type-match half is M1's, the arity/default half is MHT3211);
// ';' bodies only in interfaces/abstract hooks.

// ----- expressions -------------------------------------------------------

Expr = LiteralExpr | MagicConstExpr | InterpolatedStringExpr | HeredocExpr
     | NowdocExpr | ShellExecExpr
     | SimpleVarExpr | VarVarExpr | DynamicVarExpr | NameRef
     | ArrayExpr | ListExpr | ParenExpr
     | UnaryExpr | BinaryExpr | AssignExpr | TernaryExpr
     | PrefixIncDecExpr | PostfixIncDecExpr | CastExpr | ErrorSuppressExpr
     | InstanceofExpr | MatchExpr | CloneExpr | NewExpr | ExitExpr
     | PrintExpr | ThrowExpr | YieldExpr | YieldFromExpr | IncludeExpr
     | IssetExpr | EmptyExpr | EvalExpr
     | CallExpr | MemberAccessExpr | ScopedAccessExpr
     | SubscriptExpr
     | ClosureExpr | ArrowFnExpr
// NOTE: bare NameRef as Expr = constant fetch / fn name; 'true','false',
// 'null' live here, not in LiteralExpr — they are constants (M1 resolves).

LiteralExpr    = value:( <int> | <float> | <single_quoted> )
MagicConstExpr = token:<magic_const>

SimpleVarExpr  = var:<variable>
VarVarExpr     = '$' inner:Expr
// VALIDATE: inner restricted to variable forms ($$x, $$$x).
DynamicVarExpr = '$' '{' inner:Expr '}'
// NOTE: ${…} as a variable-variable outside strings — legal, distinct
// from the deprecated in-string form below.

ParenExpr = '(' inner:Expr ')'

UnaryExpr         = op:('+' | '-' | '!' | '~') operand:Expr
PrefixIncDecExpr  = op:('++' | '--') operand:Expr
PostfixIncDecExpr = operand:Expr! op:('++' | '--')
CastExpr          = op:( <cast> | <cast_removed> ) operand:Expr
ErrorSuppressExpr = '@' operand:Expr      // DESUGAR: severity-mask region
// 8.5 call-form: `clone($o)`, `clone($o, ['p' => v])`, named args,
// `clone(...)` FCC — a full argument list, exactly like CallExpr's
// (pinned PHP 8.5.6, burn-down 2026-06-11). LEVEL: call-form 8.5.
CloneExpr         = 'clone' ( args:ArgList | operand:Expr )
PrintExpr         = 'print' operand:Expr
ThrowExpr         = 'throw' operand:Expr  // expression since 8.0

BinaryExpr = lhs:Expr! op:BinaryOp rhs:Expr
BinaryOp = '**' | '*' | '/' | '%' | '+' | '-' | '<<' | '>>' | '.'
         | '<' | '<=' | '>' | '>=' | '==' | '!=' | '<>' | '===' | '!==' | '<=>'
         | '&' | '^' | '|' | '&&' | '||' | '??' | '|>'
         | 'and' | 'or' | 'xor'
// NOTE: precedence/associativity live in the Pratt table (M0 App. B),
// not the tree; '|>' LEVEL: 8.5. The tree is shape-faithful to whatever
// the table builds — the differential tests guard the table.

InstanceofExpr = lhs:Expr! 'instanceof' rhs:Expr
// VALIDATE: rhs restricted to class-reference forms.

AssignExpr = lhs:Expr! op:AssignOp byref:'&'? rhs:Expr
AssignOp = '=' | '+=' | '-=' | '*=' | '**=' | '/=' | '.=' | '%='
         | '&=' | '|=' | '^=' | '<<=' | '>>=' | '??='
// VALIDATE: '&' only with '='; lhs writability (incl. list/array
// destructuring on lhs — DESUGAR: indexed extraction, design doc §7.1).

TernaryExpr = cond:Expr! '?' then:Expr? ':' else_branch:Expr
// NOTE: 'then' absent = short ternary '?:'; anchors per A4 keep then/else
// unambiguous. VALIDATE: unparenthesized nesting (8.0 error, with the
// associativity explanation in the message).

MatchExpr  = 'match' '(' subject:Expr ')' '{' MatchArm,* '}'   // LEVEL: 8.0
MatchArm   = ( conds:MatchConds | 'default' ) '=>' body:Expr
MatchConds = Expr,+
// DESUGAR: decision tree with strict comparison.

NewExpr = 'new' ( anon:AnonClassDecl | ctor:Expr args:ArgList? )
// NOTE: 'new Foo()->bar()' (8.4) — postfix chains on NewExpr require
// the arg parens; the parser owns that rule, the tree just nests.
// VALIDATE: ctor restricted to class-reference forms.
AnonClassDecl : HasAttributes HasModifiers =
    'class' args:ArgList? extends:ExtendsClause? implements:ImplementsClause?
    body:ClassBody!
// NOTE: readonly anonymous classes LEVEL: 8.3.

ExitExpr = kw:('exit' | 'die') args:ArgList?
// NOTE: bare 'exit;' remains legal alongside the 8.4 function-like form.

YieldExpr     = 'yield' key:YieldKey? value:Expr?
YieldKey      = key:Expr! '=>'
YieldFromExpr = 'yield' 'from' source:Expr
IncludeExpr   = op:('include' | 'include_once' | 'require' | 'require_once') operand:Expr

IssetExpr = 'isset' '(' targets:Expr,+ ')'
EmptyExpr = 'empty' '(' target:Expr ')'
EvalExpr  = 'eval' '(' code:Expr ')'

CallExpr = callee:Expr! args:ArgList!
ArgList  = '(' Arg,* ')'
Arg      = NamedArg | SpreadArg | VariadicPlaceholder | Expr
NamedArg = name:<member_ident>! ':' value:Expr       // LEVEL: 8.0
SpreadArg = '...' value:Expr
VariadicPlaceholder = '...'                          // LEVEL: 8.1
// NOTE: f(...) first-class callable = ArgList whose sole Arg is a
// VariadicPlaceholder — VALIDATE sole-ness. NamedArg name uses
// <member_ident> as a parse superset; VALIDATE plain-ident rule.

MemberAccessExpr = obj:Expr! op:('->' | '?->') member:MemberSelector?
// NOTE: nullsafe folded as an op token; DESUGAR: guarded block (§7.1).
// VALIDATE: '?->' in write context.
ScopedAccessExpr = scope:Expr! '::' member:ScopedSelector?
MemberSelector   = MemberName | SimpleVarExpr | VarVarExpr | DynamicVarExpr | BracedMember
ScopedSelector   = MemberName | SimpleVarExpr | VarVarExpr | DynamicVarExpr | BracedMember | 'class'
BracedMember     = '{' inner:Expr '}'
// NOTE: '::class' on arbitrary objects LEVEL: 8.0; scope:Expr admits
// 'self'/'parent'/'static' as NameRef.

SubscriptExpr = base:Expr! '[' index:Expr? ']'
// NOTE: absent index = push form '$a[] = …' — legal only as write
// target (VALIDATE).
// NOTE: the curly offset '$s{0}' 8.0 removed has no rule: php's grammar
// has none, so the '{' is the token the enclosing site did not want, and
// the parser says so as php says it (design §6.1).

ArrayExpr = ( 'array' '(' ArrayElement,* ')' | '[' ArrayElement,* ']' )
ListExpr  = 'list' '(' ArrayElement,* ')'
ArrayElement = spread:'...'? key:ArrayKey? byref:'&'? value:Expr?
ArrayKey     = key:Expr! '=>'
// NOTE: fully-empty element (elision) is legal only in destructuring
// position — VALIDATE; spread excludes key/byref — VALIDATE.
// DESUGAR: ListExpr/ArrayExpr-as-lvalue → indexed extraction.

ClosureExpr : HasAttributes =
    'static'? 'function' byref:'&'? params:ParamList! uses:ClosureUseClause?
    ret:RetType? body:Block
ClosureUseClause = 'use' '(' ClosureUseVar,+ ')'
ClosureUseVar    = byref:'&'? var:<variable>!
ArrowFnExpr : HasAttributes =
    'static'? 'fn' byref:'&'? params:ParamList! ret:RetType? '=>' body:Expr
// NOTE: arrow-fn auto-capture made explicit in HIR, not here (DESUGAR);
// body extent vs ',' in arg lists is a Pratt binding-power case with
// dedicated fixtures.

// ----- string interpolation ---------------------------------------------

InterpolatedStringExpr = '"' parts:StringPart* '"'
HeredocExpr            = start:<heredoc_start> parts:StringPart* end:<heredoc_end>
NowdocExpr             = start:<heredoc_start> text:<string_text>* end:<heredoc_end>
ShellExecExpr          = '`' parts:StringPart* '`'
// DESUGAR: concatenation chain (design doc §7.1); ShellExec → shell_exec
// call. NOTE: flexible-indent strip records ride as trivia on the parts
// so reprint is byte-exact (G2) while lowering sees stripped text; an
// INDENTED nowdoc therefore carries one <string_text> per body line
// (hence `*` — adjudicated on the Symfony corpus, M0.4 burn-down).

StringPart = LiteralStringPart | SimpleInterpolation | BracedInterpolation
           | DollarBraceInterpolation
LiteralStringPart    = text:<string_text>
SimpleInterpolation  = var:<variable>! suffix:( SimpleDim | SimpleProp )?
SimpleDim  = '[' neg:'-'? index:( <ident> | <variable> | <encaps_int> | <int> ) ']'
// NOTE: `neg` is php's `'-' T_NUM_STRING` branch of encaps_var_offset
// (zend_negate_num_string): "$a[-1]" and "$a[1]" compile differently, so
// the sign is a field beside the digits. The parser admits '-' before
// <encaps_int> and <int> only, as php's grammar does.
SimpleProp = op:('->' | '?->') name:<ident>!
// NOTE: the deliberately restricted in-string grammar — bare-word keys,
// no expressions, single property hop ('->' or '?->': the nullsafe simple
// form interpolates on the 8.3 reference — G3 adjudication). Richer needs:
BracedInterpolation     = '{' inner:Expr '}'           // lexer guarantees '{$'
DollarBraceInterpolation = '${' ( name:<ident> dim:SimpleDim? | inner:Expr ) '}'
// VALIDATE: deprecation diagnostic (8.2) on every use, both forms.

// ----- shared small lists -------------------------------------------------
// (Expr,* / Expr,+ inline per A2; no standalone ExprList node — sites that
// need stable span homes define wrappers, per A4.)

